{
  "name": "Infisical v4",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "source": "Infisical v4 design system"
  },
  "themes": {
    "note": "A theme is a named palette with a scheme (light or dark). Every themed token keeps a light and a dark base value. A theme either sits on one of those base columns (base) or extends another theme (extends), and lists in overrides only the tokens whose values differ. A token resolves to the nearest override on the way down the extends chain, then to the base column the chain ends on. Themes of the same scheme are interchangeable: anything that branches on light or dark reads the scheme, never the theme name.",
    "list": [
      {
        "id": "peach",
        "name": "Lightly Peach",
        "scheme": "light",
        "base": "light",
        "overrides": {
          "sidebar": "#f5f3ee",
          "inset": "#ffffff",
          "surface": "#ffffff",
          "tint": "#faf8f4",
          "line": "#d5cdc2",
          "line-soft": "#e4ded5",
          "faint": "#85807a",
          "mix-ink": "#2e271d"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "pale",
        "name": "Light",
        "scheme": "light",
        "base": "light",
        "overrides": {
          "sidebar": "#efeff0",
          "inset": "#f9f9fa",
          "surface": "#ffffff",
          "tint": "#f3f3f3",
          "line": "#cbcbcf",
          "line-soft": "#dadadd",
          "faint": "#828387"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "dark",
        "name": "Dark",
        "scheme": "dark",
        "base": "dark",
        "overrides": {
          "sidebar": "#09090a",
          "inset": "#121213",
          "sidebar-hover": "color-mix(in srgb, {mix-ink} {current-mix}, {frame})"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "color": {
    "note": "Neutral first. Ink on warm off-white, one accent (Infisical yellow #e3f047, the same in both themes), status colors that always travel with a word or icon. The app is a sidebar beside an inset, both light in light and both dark in dark. Dark mirrors light: ink becomes bone, the accent takes over the on switch and the mark, and selection stays neutral.",
    "tokens": [
      {
        "name": "frame",
        "value": {
          "light": "#010101",
          "dark": "#010101"
        },
        "usage": "Near-black ground. The dark-theme sidebar sits on it (through sidebar); in light the sidebar is light and nothing in the app shell uses frame. It never wraps the inset. Never put text on it except inside the sidebar."
      },
      {
        "name": "frame-soft",
        "value": {
          "light": "#ecebe5",
          "dark": "#010101"
        },
        "usage": "Warm ground for embedded views and docs that want a frame around their content. In dark it matches frame."
      },
      {
        "name": "surface",
        "value": {
          "light": "#fbfbf9",
          "dark": "#111111"
        },
        "usage": "The main panel and every inset card and input. Menus, popovers and dialogs float on pop. The default ground for text. A step above inset in both themes, so cards read on the page without a bright border."
      },
      {
        "name": "pop",
        "value": {
          "light": "{surface}",
          "dark": "{surface}"
        },
        "usage": "Ground of everything that floats above the page: menus, listboxes, popovers, hover cards, dialogs, sheets. Equal to surface, as in the v4 reference: a panel separates from the page through pop-line and shadow-pop, never through a brighter fill. Always with pop-line and shadow-pop."
      },
      {
        "name": "pop-line",
        "value": {
          "light": "{line-soft}",
          "dark": "{line-soft}"
        },
        "usage": "The 1px edge of a pop panel, drawn as a ring inside its shadow. Uses line-soft, the default outward-facing border, and the shadow carries the separation from the page."
      },
      {
        "name": "inset",
        "value": {
          "light": "{surface}",
          "dark": "#0b0b0b"
        },
        "usage": "The app's page ground beside the sidebar, behind cards, tables and lists. Equal to surface in light, as in the v4 reference, and a step below it in dark (1.04:1), so a card separates from the page through its line-soft edge and frame rather than a ground step. Pads space-40 (bottom space-48)."
      },
      {
        "name": "sidebar",
        "value": {
          "light": "{tint}",
          "dark": "{frame}"
        },
        "usage": "Ground of the app sidebar. tint in light (1.1:1 against the inset, so it needs its line-soft edge) and frame in dark. Text on it uses ink, text2 and muted: muted is 6.4:1 in light and 9.6:1 in dark. The current page is sidebar-current with ink text; counts are accent Counts, and a rail dot, which has no number, is accent-fg."
      },
      {
        "name": "sidebar-current",
        "value": {
          "light": "color-mix(in srgb, {mix-ink} {current-mix}, {sidebar})",
          "dark": "color-mix(in srgb, {mix-ink} {current-mix}, {sidebar})"
        },
        "usage": "The current page in the sidebar, and a rail group that holds it: mix-ink at current-mix mixed opaquely into the sidebar (5.5% in light, 10% in dark), a small step past the shared hover overlay at hover-mix, so it follows every theme's sidebar with no per-theme value. Neutral, like every selection; in the sidebar only counts take the accent."
      },
      {
        "name": "sidebar-hover",
        "value": {
          "light": "{sidebar-current}",
          "dark": "{sidebar-current}"
        },
        "usage": "The sidebar's hover highlight, the block that follows the pointer between rows. It matches sidebar-current unless a theme quiets it: Dark mixes current-mix into frame rather than its lifted sidebar, so hovering a row is a softer step than the current page."
      },
      {
        "name": "paper",
        "value": {
          "light": "#f4f3ee",
          "dark": "#161616"
        },
        "usage": "Dialog and sheet footers. A step off surface so the action bar reads as a shelf."
      },
      {
        "name": "tint",
        "value": {
          "light": "#f1f0ea",
          "dark": "#1c1c1c"
        },
        "usage": "Borderless shells around bordered inset surfaces (cards, tables, lists), table headers, segmented tracks, disabled and read-only fields, the hover ground of striped table rows, and the light sidebar (through sidebar). In dark it is lifted so a borderless shell still reads against surface (1.11:1)."
      },
      {
        "name": "row-done",
        "value": {
          "light": "#f6f5f1",
          "dark": "#101010"
        },
        "usage": "Resolved list items that stay in place so nothing jumps."
      },
      {
        "name": "row-done-card",
        "value": {
          "light": "color-mix(in oklab, {tint} 50%, transparent)",
          "dark": "color-mix(in oklab, {tint} 50%, transparent)"
        },
        "usage": "Resolved rows in a segmented List: half the tint card fill, so a resolved card stays in place and keeps its edge on the page in both themes, where row-done would vanish in dark."
      },
      {
        "name": "row-done-divided",
        "value": {
          "light": "color-mix(in oklab, {ink} 4%, transparent)",
          "dark": "color-mix(in oklab, {ink} 6%, transparent)"
        },
        "usage": "Resolved rows in a divided List, which sit on the page with no container: translucent ink over whatever ground is behind (1.09:1 on the light page, 1.11:1 on the dark one), a clear step where row-done would vanish in dark and still quieter than hover (1.14:1 light, 1.33:1 dark)."
      },
      {
        "name": "select",
        "value": {
          "light": "#eeede6",
          "dark": "#262626"
        },
        "usage": "Selection in connected rows: a list's current and checked rows, selected table and tree rows, DataGrid ranges, the pressed toggle Button. On rows it is the whole signal, with the row text one step up (text2 to ink, muted to text2); no edge bar. Neutral in both themes, never tinted: in dark it is 1.25:1 on surface and a step above tint (1.13:1), the same step as before."
      },
      {
        "name": "line-soft",
        "value": {
          "light": "#e6e5e0",
          "dark": "#1e2022"
        },
        "usage": "The default border: the outward-facing edge of inset surfaces, cards, plain lists, tables, popovers, dialogs and bordered controls that use a line token, the app shell chrome (the AppInset island border, the narrow TopBar rule, the sidebar edge, corner and section separators), and every divider that touches one of those edges, such as row hairlines, table cell dividers and dialog head and footer rules. Frames have no border; only the inset surface inside them carries line-soft. Also skeleton blocks, progress tracks and soft badges."
      },
      {
        "name": "line",
        "value": {
          "light": "#d8d8d4",
          "dark": "#2f3234"
        },
        "usage": "Reserved for a standalone rule that touches no other border: a section rule, the band's divider marks (through crumb-divider), a lone hr, a tree guide, the tab track, chart axes and grid lines. One step stronger than line-soft, so a free-standing line still reads without an edge to lean on. Never the edge of a surface or a divider that meets one; those are line-soft."
      },
      {
        "name": "control",
        "value": {
          "light": "#b0b0a9",
          "dark": "#37393c"
        },
        "usage": "Borders of inputs, selects and secondary buttons. Source pair: 2.1:1 on surface in light and 1.6:1 in dark, below the 3:1 floor for control borders. Kept exact; focus turns the border ink with a 3px nudge outline. An invalid field rests on bad-control and turns bad with the 3px bad outline while focused."
      },
      {
        "name": "crumb-divider",
        "value": {
          "light": "{line}",
          "dark": "{line}"
        },
        "usage": "The vertical divider between breadcrumb crumbs, in the TopBar and in page and folder trails. line, the standalone-rule tint: each divider is a lone mark that touches no other border, one step stronger than the line-soft shell chrome around it. Decorative: it never carries meaning."
      },
      {
        "name": "faint",
        "value": {
          "light": "#8e9291",
          "dark": "#8e9291"
        },
        "usage": "Disabled text only; breadcrumb dividers use crumb-divider. 3.0:1 on surface in light (6.0:1 in dark): never for text people must read."
      },
      {
        "name": "muted",
        "value": {
          "light": "#565654",
          "dark": "#b0b0a9"
        },
        "usage": "Secondary text, descriptions, placeholders, eyebrows and captions. 7.1:1 on surface, 6.4:1 on tint in light; 8.7:1 and 7.8:1 in dark."
      },
      {
        "name": "text2",
        "value": {
          "light": "#2f3234",
          "dark": "#d8d8d4"
        },
        "usage": "Body copy that sits one step below ink: descriptions in alerts, table cells, ghost button labels. 12.5:1 on surface in light, 13.8:1 in dark."
      },
      {
        "name": "ink",
        "value": {
          "light": "#010101",
          "dark": "#f1f0ea"
        },
        "usage": "Primary text and icons on surface, tint, paper and select (at least 17:1 in light, 13:1 in dark). Also the fill of checked controls and person avatars."
      },
      {
        "name": "mix-ink",
        "value": {
          "light": "{ink}",
          "dark": "{ink}"
        },
        "usage": "The neutral every hover, press and current mix takes in, so state grounds shift the surface underneath without leaving its family. ink by default; peach overrides it with a dark warm neutral from its own hue (#2e271d), so states blend into the warm ground instead of greying it."
      },
      {
        "name": "on-ink",
        "value": {
          "light": "#ffffff",
          "dark": "#010101"
        },
        "usage": "Text and icons on an ink fill: checked checkboxes, person avatars, tooltips."
      },
      {
        "name": "accent",
        "value": {
          "light": "#e3f047",
          "dark": "#e3f047"
        },
        "usage": "The one accent, Infisical yellow #e3f047 in both themes. The fill of the one primary create action on a page (Add new, Create key, New connection), approval and grant buttons, counts (in the sidebar and the bulk action bar), the on switch track in dark, the slider range in dark and search highlights; the current page in the sidebar stays neutral. On light grounds the fill is nearly as light as the ground (1.09:1 on the sidebar, 1.20:1 on surface) and carries no edge: it is a highlight, and what it says is its on-accent text (16.7:1 on it), so the label, not the fill, identifies the control or the number. Never let a bare fill with no text carry meaning (a dot, a bar); use accent-fg for those. In dark it stands out on its own (16.7:1 on the sidebar, 15.1:1 on surface). A fill, never text on light grounds. For accent-colored text and icons (the banner), use accent-fg."
      },
      {
        "name": "accent-2",
        "value": {
          "light": "#d3df29",
          "dark": "#d1de23"
        },
        "usage": "Hover and pressed fill of accent buttons. A step darker than accent on the same hue; on-accent on it is 14.3:1 in light and 14.1:1 in dark."
      },
      {
        "name": "on-accent",
        "value": {
          "light": "#010101",
          "dark": "#010101"
        },
        "usage": "Text and icons on an accent fill: near-black in both themes, because the fill does not change with theme (16.7:1 on accent; 14.3:1 on accent-2 in light, 14.1:1 in dark)."
      },
      {
        "name": "accent-wash",
        "value": {
          "light": "#f7fbc9",
          "dark": "#1a1c0d"
        },
        "usage": "Very light accent ground for a highlighted row, a callout and the production banner. Text on it is ink (19.5:1 light, 15.1:1 dark)."
      },
      {
        "name": "accent-line",
        "value": {
          "light": "#dede88",
          "dark": "#3a401c"
